{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1090","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1090","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1090\",\"parent_revision\":\"9003e5c0b1eba2ce072fcc4f01b68f224c8f2955b88370871905d072aa36bc39\",\"root_revision\":\"9003e5c0b1eba2ce072fcc4f01b68f224c8f2955b88370871905d072aa36bc39\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWhen mark_groomed=True and find_item(fresh_items, selector) returns None after parse_backlog(), neither local frontmatter nor GitHub label update happens. No warning is emitted and no result key indicates the skip. Violates silent-failure-prevention rule.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaim 1: `groom_item` uses `find_item(fresh_items, selector)` in mark_groomed block and when it returns None, neither local nor GitHub update happens with no warning\\n\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEvidence:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py, lines 3387-3400\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-16\\n  - Content: |\\n      if mark_groomed and \\\"error\\\" not in result:\\n          fresh_items = parse_backlog()\\n          fresh_item = find_item(fresh_items, selector)\\n          if fresh_item and fresh_item.file_path:\\n              update_item_metadata(Path(fresh_item.file_path), {\\\"metadata\\\": {\\\"status\\\": \\\"groomed\\\"}}, output=out)\\n              result[\\\"mark_groomed_applied\\\"] = True\\n              out.info(\\\"  Status: groomed (local)\\\")\\n          if fresh_item and fresh_item.issue:\\n              try:\\n                  apply_status_groomed(fresh_item, repo, output=out)\\n              except GithubException as e:\\n                  out.warn(f\\\"  GitHub label update failed: {e}\\\")\\n                  result[\\\"mark_groomed_label_error\\\"] = str(e)\\n      return result\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/rules/silent-failure-prevention.md, section \\\"Branching on Input Values Requires an Explicit Fallback\\\"\\n  - Finding: Rule explicitly requires that branches on input values (including the result of `find_item()`) must have a final fallback branch that either acts or errors. Falling through without logging is a silent data loss bug.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: When `find_item` returns `None`, both the `if fresh_item and fresh_item.file_path:` condition (line 3390) and the `if fresh_item and fresh_item.issue:` condition (line 3394) evaluate to False. Execution falls through to `return result` with no warning or error recorded. This violates the \\\"Branching on Input Values Requires an Explicit Fallback\\\" pattern from silent-failure-prevention.md, which requires fallback branches for unknown/edge-case conditions.\\n\\n---\\n\\nClaim 2: No existing test covers the case where `find_item` returns None in mark_groomed re-lookup path\\n\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEvidence:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_groom_mark_groomed.py\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-16\\n  - Content: Full file reviewed (105 lines total). Test file contains:\\n    * test_resolve_groomed_content_raises_without_input (lines 34-46)\\n    * test_groom_item_mark_groomed_no_content_does_not_call_update_item (lines 54-78)\\n    * test_groom_item_mark_groomed_with_content_calls_update_item (lines 81-104)\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: Grep search for \\\"fresh_item = None|when.*find_item.*returns None\\\" in /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/\\n  - Finding: No matches found in any test file. The existing tests mock `find_item` to return a fake_item with `file_path=None` and `issue=None`, but never test the case where `find_item` returns `None` itself.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The current test in line 54-78 mocks `find_item` to return a `MagicMock` item with `file_path=None` and `issue=None`, which is different from testing the case where `find_item()` returns `None` entirely. The comment on line 69 acknowledges that \\\"the mark_groomed path tries a second parse_backlog + find_item\\\", but the test does not cover the failure case where that second `find_item` lookup returns `None`.\\n\\n---\\n\\nClaim 3: Violated design rule is \\\"Branching on Input Values Requires an Explicit Fallback\\\" from silent-failure-prevention.md\\n\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED\\n\\nEvidence:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/rules/silent-failure-prevention.md, lines 40-66\\n  - Retrieved: 2026-04-16\\n  - Content: |\\n      ## Branching on Input Values Requires an Explicit Fallback\\n\\n      Every `if`/`elif` chain or match on an input value must have a final branch that either acts or errors. Falling through to `return unchanged` without logging is a silent data loss bug.\\n\\n      **Wrong:**\\n\\n      ```python\\n      if name in KNOWN_SECTIONS:\\n          return replace_section(body, name, content)\\n      # BUG: unknown name silently returns body unchanged\\n      return body\\n      ```\\n\\n      **Right:**\\n\\n      ```python\\n      if name in SPECIAL_SECTIONS:\\n          return replace_special(body, name, content)\\n      # Fallback: treat as generic section\\n      return replace_generic(body, name, content)\\n      ```\\n\\n      If no fallback action is possible, raise or warn:\\n\\n      ```python\\n      raise ValueError(f\\\"Unrecognized section: {name}\\\")\\n      ```\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n  - Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py, lines 3389-3400 (the groom_item mark_groomed block)\\n  - Finding: The structure matches the \\\"Wrong\\\" example in the rule: `fresh_item = find_item(...)` is checked with `if fresh_item and ...`, but when `fresh_item is None`, there is no fallback branch. The function falls through and returns result without logging the failure or raising an error.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The groom_item function at lines 3389-3394 demonstrates exactly the pattern the silent-failure-prevention rule prohibits. The rule requires that when an input value (result of `find_item()`) is checked in an `if` statement, there must be a final `else` or fallback branch that either acts, logs, or raises. Here, when `fresh_item is None`, the mark_groomed status advance silently fails with no warning to the user.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:3387-3400 (accessed 2026-04-16)\\n  SOURCE: /home/user/claude_skills/backlog_core/tests/test_groom_mark_groomed.py (accessed 2026-04-16)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read on 2026-04-16\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final Assessment: fix: groom_item mark_groomed silently skips status advance when item re-resolve fails\\nDate: 2026-04-16\\nGoal: Fix groom_item to emit a warning and set an explicit skip signal when mark_groomed=True but the post-write re-parsed item lookup returns None.\\n\\nConditions (information completeness only \u2014 deliverables moved to Acceptance Criteria):\\n1. Bug location confirmed: operations.py:3387-3400 \u2014 both `if fresh_item and ...` guards silently skip when find_item returns None | Status: AVAILABLE\\n   Evidence: Code:plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:3387-3400\\n2. All call sites using mark_groomed=True identified: server.py:2132 (via operations.groom_item) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n   Evidence: Code search confirmed\\n3. Existing test coverage paths mapped: test_groom_mark_groomed.py + TestGroomItemMarkGroomed class | Status: AVAILABLE\\n   Evidence: Code:backlog_core/tests/test_groom_mark_groomed.py:1-105\\n4. Missing test path confirmed: no test covers fresh_item=None re-lookup failure in mark_groomed block | Status: AVAILABLE\\n   Evidence: Full inspection of all mark_groomed tests \u2014 none test None re-lookup\\n5. Fix API contract 