do not exercise the mark_groomed block internals\\n\\n### Documentation\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` (lines 265-277) - Section \\\"Status advancement via `mark_groomed`\\\" documents three transitions (local frontmatter, label removal, label add). The section \\\"Error handling\\\" (line 275) states \\\"If the GitHub label transition fails, the local frontmatter update still applies and a warning is recorded in the result.\\\" No mention of the case where `find_item` returns `None` and the entire status transition is skipped. After the fix, a new failure path exists (`mark_groomed_skipped=True` + warning) that must be documented here alongside the existing GitHub label failure path. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Documentation of the `mark_groomed` behavior will be incomplete/misleading after the fix ships; agents and humans relying on this doc would not know to check for the new skip key\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md` (lines 198-224) - Describes `mark_groomed=True` behavior and the \\\"Groomed\\\" terminal state. Documents that the status transition fires atomically after the batch write. Does not document what happens when the post-write re-parse fails to find the item. After the fix, the workflow should note that a `mark_groomed_skipped` key in the response signals failure and requires operator attention (the item was written but not status-advanced). | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Agent-facing workflow document; groomer agents following this doc would not know to inspect for `mark_groomed_skipped` and handle it\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n- None identified.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md` (line 158) - Instructs the agent: \\\"the groomer teammate runs after you and is responsible for the mark_groomed=True call.\\\" No behavioral change from this fix \u2014 the instruction remains accurate. The rtica-assessor does not inspect `mark_groomed_applied` or any result key. | Risk: LOW | Why: Instruction is about delegation responsibility, not result-key inspection; unaffected by new key\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-output-validation.md` (line 90) - States the blocked path does not call `backlog_groom(mark_groomed=True)`. This is unchanged by the fix. However, the document does not describe what to do if `mark_groomed=True` is called but returns `mark_groomed_skipped=True`. After the fix, groomer agents would benefit from a note that a `mark_groomed_skipped` response key signals the status advance did not apply and may require a retry or manual intervention. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Agent-facing validation reference; groomer agents that check the response would silently miss the skip signal without updated guidance\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` | Role: producer | Connection: Contains `groom_item` \u2014 the function being fixed | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` | Role: consumer | Connection: Calls `operations.groom_item(mark_groomed=...)` and forwards result dict to MCP callers | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_groom_mark_groomed.py` | Role: test | Connection: Regression tests for the mark_groomed block; no test covers `find_item` returning None | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` | Role: test | Connection: Integration tests for `TestGroomItemMarkGroomed`; same coverage gap | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` | Role: test | Connection: MCP-layer forwarding tests; mock-based, unaffected | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: Documents