 Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix: groom_item mark_groomed silently skips status advance when item re-resolve fails** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Quality vigilance concern from #1078, code review by code-reviewer on T1\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-16)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nCall `groom_item()` with `mark_groomed=True` against an item whose selector matches a known item in the pre-write item list but does not appear in the re-fetched `fresh_items` list (e.g., due to a GitHub API fetch failure or a cache miss). Observe that the function returns without warning, without updating the local frontmatter status to `groomed`, and without applying the `status:groomed` GitHub label. No error is raised; no warning appears in the returned `messages` or `warnings` lists; no result key indicates the skip occurred.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n4/10 \u2014 P2.\\n\\nThe bug affects a code path that is only active when `mark_groomed=True` is passed AND the re-lookup of the item in the freshly fetched list fails. In normal operation, the re-lookup succeeds. The silent skip is harmful when it does trigger because callers (human or agent) receive a success-shaped response while the item's status has not advanced, leading to divergence between perceived and actual state. Severity is moderate: no data is destroyed and the content write itself succeeds; only the status-advance is lost. Frequency is low under normal network conditions but rises when GitHub API calls are degraded or when the item was recently renamed.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nWhen the bug triggers, the following observable problems occur:\\n\\n- The item's local frontmatter status remains at whatever value it held before the call \u2014 it is not advanced to `groomed`.\\n- The `status:needs-grooming` GitHub label is not removed and the `status:groomed` label is not applied.\\n- The caller (human or agent) receives no indication that the status advance was skipped. The response looks identical to a fully successful call.\\n- Downstream pipeline stages that check item status to decide whether grooming is complete will incorrectly conclude the item still needs grooming, or will silently proceed with stale status, depending on their logic.\\n- The groomer agent cannot distinguish a successful `mark_groomed` from a silently skipped one without re-reading the item's frontmatter or GitHub labels separately.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Callers that pass `mark_groomed=True` receive an explicit, inspectable signal when the status advance did not occur, enabling them to retry, report, or halt rather than continue with incorrect assumptions.\\n- The grooming pipeline becomes auditable: every `groom_item` result either confirms status was advanced or explains why it was not.\\n- Agents and humans can trust the response shape of `groom_item` without a secondary verification read of item state.\\n- The fix aligns `groom_item` with the silent-failure-prevention rule applied consistently elsewhere in the codebase, removing an inconsistency that could mislead future contributors.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `mark_groomed=True` is passed and the re-lookup of the item returns `None`, `groom_item` should:\\n\\n1. Emit a warning (via `out.warn()`) stating that the status advance was skipped because the item could not be re-resolved, including the selector used for the lookup.\\n2. Include `mark_groomed_skipped=True` in the returned result dict so callers can branch on it.\\n3. Include `mark_groomed_skip_reason` in the returned result dict with enough context (the selector) to diagnose the failure.\\n4. Return normally (not raise an exception) so that the already-written groomed content is not lost.\\n\\nUnder normal operation (re-lookup succeeds), behavior is unchanged.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `groom_item` emits `out.warn(...)` when `find_item(fresh_items, selector)` returns `None` in the `mark_groomed` block\\n- [ ] `result[\\\"mark_groomed_skipped\\\"] = True` is set when the re-lookup returns `None`\\n- [ ] `result[\\\"mark_groomed_skip_reason\\\"]` contains the selector value to aid debugging\\n- [ ] Existing `TestGroomItemMarkGroomed` tests all still pass\\n- [ ] New test `test_groom_item_mark_groomed_skipped_when_item_not_found_after_reparse` is added and passes\\n- [ ] `backlog-item-lifecycle.md` updated to document `mark_groomed_skipped` response key\\n- [ ] `finalize.md` updated to instruct groomer agents to inspect for `mark_groomed_skipped` in the MCP response\\n- [ ] `groomer-output-validation.md` updated with the new skip-signal handling\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` exits 0\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|---|---|\\n| Rule | `.claude/rules/silent-failure-prevention.md` \u2014 \\\"Branching on Input Values Requires an Explicit Fallback\\\" |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 `groom_item()` implementation |\\n| Test file | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_groom_mark_groomed.py` \u2014 existing coverage baseline |\\n| Doc | `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` |\\n| Doc | `plugins/development-harness/docs/finalize.md` |\\n| Doc | `plugins/development-harness/docs/groomer-output-validation.md` |\\n| Prior issue | #1078 \u2014 quality vigilance concern that surfaced this defect |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n| Role | File | Change needed |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Code \u2014 bug site | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` (lines 3387-3400) | CODE_CHANGE \u2014 add warn + result keys when fresh_item is None |\\n| Consumer \u2014 verify compatibility | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` (`backlog_groom` handler) | VERIFY_COMPATIBLE \u2014 additive result keys only; no breaking change expected |\\n| Tests | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_groom_mark_groomed.py`, `TestGroomItemMarkGroomed` | TEST_UPDATE \u2014 add regression test for fresh_item=None path |\\n| Docs | `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` | CONTENT_UPDATE |\\n| Docs | `plugins/development-harness/docs/finalize.md` | CONTENT_UPDATE |\\n| Docs | `plugins/development-harness/docs/groomer-output-validation.md` | CONTENT_UPDATE |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 the bug site, test file, and doc files are all present and independently accessible.\\n- Blocks: None identified \u2014 no open backlog items are known to be waiting on this fix.\\n- Related: #1078 (quality vigilance concern that identified this defect; already closed or tracked separately).\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall.\\n\\nThe bug is precisely located (operations.py:3387-3400), the fix is additive (emit warn, set two result keys), no interface contracts change, and one new test covers the missing path. Three doc files require content updates but none require structural changes. Total scope is one function, one test class, and three doc sections.\\n\\n### Description\\n\\n`groom_item()` in `backlog_core/operations.py:3387-3400` uses `find_item(fresh_items, selector)` after a post-write `parse_backlog()` re-parse to locate the item before advancing its status. When this re-lookup returns `None`, both the local frontmatter update and the GitHub label transition are silently skipped. The caller receives no warning and no result key indicates the skip occurred, violating the \\\"Branching on Input Values Requires an Explicit Fallback\\\" rule from `.claude/rules/silent-failure-prevention.md`.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n\\n**Rationale**: Observable failure with traceable cause chain. The code path is identifiable (operations.py:3387-3400), the condition is reproducible (fresh_item = None after re-parse), and the broken behavior is verifiable (silent skip with no warning or result key). Decision tree: Q1=No (not procedural), Q2=No (no prior similar failures in backlog), Q3=Yes (traceable failure) \u2192 defect.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys via /find-cause skill + code inspection\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: When mark_groomed=True is passed to groom_item() and the post-write re-lookup of the item fails (find_item returns None), the status advance is silently skipped with no warning to the user \u2192 When mark_groomed=True, an explicit warning is emitted if the re-lookup fails, and the failure is recorded in the result dict so the caller knows the mark_groomed advance was not applied.\\n\\n### Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n**Method**: 5-whys via /find-cause skill\\n\\n**Evidence chain**:\\n1. Observed failure: When mark_groomed=True, the status advance to \\\"groomed\\\" is silently skipped when find_item(fresh_items, selector) returns None after re-parse\\n2. Why: The mark_groomed block uses guard conditions `if fresh_item and fresh_item.file_path:` and `if fresh_item and fresh_item.issue:` but does not handle the case where fresh_item is None\\n3. Why: Both guards short-circuit on fresh_item being None, leaving execution to fall through to return result with no warning or error\\n4. Why: The code assumes find_item(fresh_items, selector) always returns a non-None value, but it can return None when the selector does not match any item in the re-parsed items\\n5. Why: The design pattern uses implicit None-handling (via and guards) instead of explicit fallback branches for the None case, violating the silent-failure-prevention rule\\n\\n**Root cause**: The mark_groomed path lacks an explicit else/fallback branch when fresh_item is None. When the re-lookup fails, no warning is emitted and no result key indicates the failure, causing the skip to be silent.\\n\\n**Fix locus**: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:3387-3400` \u2014 Add an else block after the two if conditions to emit a warning and set result[\\\"mark_groomed_skipped\\\"] = True when fresh_item is None.\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| task-plan | plan/P1083-auto-advance-mark-groomed-silent-failure-fix.yaml | current |  | 2026-03-28T14:37:52Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"69c5b50a7b3606abed7d8d605606018fe8a522b3c69a63af61fee42a8b02f0b1\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCuSRA\"}"}